--- O-1  Load it. Nothing here has been parsed. Three prelude signatures
---      should be confirmed on the first load, since the specification will
---      not typecheck if any differs:
---        * sd : Nat Nat -> Nat                              (module NAT)
---        * _^_ : NzNat Nat -> NzNat, needed so that the modulus in
---          trailingSignificand is accepted by _rem_ : Nat NzNat -> Nat
---        * string : Rat Nat ~> String                (module CONVERSION)
---      If the third differs, only P3109-NAMING is affected.
---
--- O-2  Confirm that every import is genuinely protecting (review finding
---      R-5). Maude does not check import modes; they are claims.
---
--- O-3  3.1 NOTE 2 gives two concrete encodings -- 2.0 in Binary8p4se is
---      code point 0x48, and Inf in Binary8p4se is 0x7F. Neither can be
---      discharged here, because both depend on the encoding that NOTE 3
---      defers to 4.7.6. They are recorded as tests to run once that clause
---      is in scope:
---        codeOf(encode(b8p4se, 2)) == 72
---        codeOf(encode(b8p4se, posInfinity)) == 127
---      Until then the terms do not reduce, which is the correct behaviour
---      and not a defect.
---
--- O-4  Confluence and termination are argued informally above (twoPow
---      decreases |N|; every other equation is non-recursive; the guards of
---      each conditional group are mutually exclusive). Confirm with Maude's
---      Church-Rosser and termination tools rather than by inspection.
 tw